From: Kelvin Jiang <kelvinjiang@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:26:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] [M156] [Extensions] Validate UTF-8 and duplicate rule IDs
 in RulesRegistry

Original change's description:
> [Extensions] Validate UTF-8 and duplicate rule IDs in RulesRegistry
>
> Rule IDs containing invalid UTF-8 (such as lone UTF-16 surrogates
> encoded as WTF-8) can collapse to identical U+FFFD replacement sequences
> when serialized to JSON in StateStore. On startup replay,
> RulesRegistry::DeserializeAndAddRules() called AddRulesNoFill() without
> checking for intra-batch duplicate IDs, allowing duplicate rule IDs to
> reach subclass AddRulesImpl() implementations.
>
> Harden declarative rule registration across RulesRegistry and its
> subclasses:
> 1. Reject non-UTF-8 rule IDs (via
>    base::IsStringUTF8AllowingNoncharacters) and validate intra-batch
>    uniqueness before mutating used_rule_identifiers_ in
>    CheckAndFillInOptionalRules() and in AddRulesNoFill().
> 2. Convert error strings in RulesRegistry::ReportInternalError() with
>    base::UTF8ToUTF16() instead of base::ASCIIToUTF16() so non-ASCII
>    duplicate rule IDs do not trip ASCII DCHECKs.
> 3. Enforce UTF-8 validity, intra-batch uniqueness, and ownership commit
>    before predicate/trigger indexing in ChromeContentRulesRegistry and
>    WebRequestRulesRegistry, and upgrade WebRequestRulesRegistry's
>    RuleTriggers to raw_ptr declared after webrequest_rules_.
>
